kind: theorem
title: "The mean value inequality: if $f : [a,b] \\to \\mathbb{R}^m$ is continuous and differentiable on $(a,b)$ with $\\lVert f'\\rVert_2 \\le M$, then $\\lVert f(b)-f(a)\\rVert_2 \\le M(b-a)$"
status: published
origin: session
provenance:
